3.4 KNN pixel classification (Lab 8)
The Lab 8 KNN experiment is supervised classification at the pixel level. Training samples are manually clicked from red pepper, 
green pepper, yellow pepper and background. Each sample is represented by three RGB features.
n = 5;
[x,y] = ginput(n);
Red = zeros(n,3);
for i=1:n
 Red(i,:) = double(reshape(RGB(round(y(i)),round(x(i)),:),1,3));
end
trainData = [Red; Green; Yellow; Background];
trainLabel = [ones(n,1); 2*ones(n,1); 3*ones(n,1); 4*ones(n,1)];
Mdl = fitcknn(trainData,trainLabel,'NumNeighbors',3);
X = double(reshape(RGB,[],3));
label = predict(Mdl,X);
L = reshape(label,size(RGB,1),size(RGB,2));
Limitation of pixel-wise KNN. RGB-only KNN ignores neighbourhood and object shape. Pixels of different objects can share 
similar colours, and illumination can change RGB values. Spatial smoothing, morphology, richer features, colour-space changes 
or learned models can improve robustness.

